# Audio & MIDI Rules

## Audio Recording (useAudioRecorder.ts)
- Do NOT use MediaRecorder API for recording. Browsers output webm/opus (Chrome) or mp4/aac (Safari), not WAV. Music production needs lossless WAV.
- Instead: use an AudioWorklet to capture raw PCM Float32 samples from the mic.
- After recording, encode PCM to WAV format manually (write RIFF/WAV header + PCM data).
- Store the resulting WAV Blob in IdeaMedia with mimeType 'audio/wav'.
- Flow: navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia({ audio: true }) → AudioContext → AudioWorkletNode (PCM capture) → on stop, encode to WAV Blob.
- Always handle permission denial gracefully (user denies mic access).
- Display a waveform during and after recording. Use the PCM data or AnalyserNode for visualization.

## MIDI Recording (useMidi.ts)
- Use Web MIDI API directly (navigator.requestMIDIAccess()). No wrapper library needed.
- Feature-detect first: if requestMIDIAccess is undefined, show "MIDI not supported in this browser" message. Do not crash.
- List available MIDI inputs. Let user select one.
- On midimessage events, parse note-on (status 0x90, velocity > 0) and note-off (status 0x80 or 0x90 with velocity 0).
- During recording, simultaneously play each note through the synth engine (useSynth) so the user hears what they play.
- After recording, store NoteEvent[] and serialize to Standard MIDI File via @tonejs/midi.
- Store as IdeaMedia with type 'midi', blob = .mid file, noteData = NoteEvent[].

## Synth Engine (useSynth.ts)
- Two layers: Tone.js for synthesis, smplr for sample-based instrument playback.
- ~10 patches available: Piano, Electric Piano, Bass, Synth Bass, Brass, Strings, Synth Lead, Synth Pad, Organ, Mallet.
- Use smplr with FluidR3_GM or MusyngKite soundfonts for realistic instrument sounds. Load soundfonts on demand (lazy), not all at startup.
- Fall back to Tone.js built-in synths (Synth, FMSynth, AMSynth, etc.) if soundfont hasn't loaded yet.
- Tone.js AudioContext must be started on a user gesture (click/tap) — browser autoplay policy. Call Tone.start() on the first user interaction.
- Provide a simple interface: playSingleNote(pitch, duration, patch), playNoteSequence(notes[], patch), stopAll().

## Audio-to-MIDI (useAudioToMidi.ts)
- Uses @spotify/basic-pitch (basic-pitch-ts on npm).
- Runs entirely client-side via TensorFlow.js. No server.
- The model file loads on first use and should be cached. Show a loading indicator.
- Input: AudioBuffer (decode the audio blob first via AudioContext.decodeAudioData).
- basic-pitch downmixes to mono and resamples to 22050 Hz internally.
- Output: note events with pitch, onset, duration. Convert to NoteEvent[] format.
- Notes are unquantized — they represent real timing, not snapped to a grid.
- Works for melodic/polyphonic content. Does NOT detect drums/percussion.
- After extraction, create a new IdeaMedia (type: 'midi') linked to the same Idea as the source audio.
- Let user preview the extracted MIDI before confirming.

## MIDI File I/O (src/lib/midi.ts)
- Use @tonejs/midi for reading and writing Standard MIDI Files.
- Import: parse .mid file → extract NoteEvent[] → store in IdeaMedia.noteData.
- Export: convert NoteEvent[] → @tonejs/midi Midi object → write to Blob.
- Exported .mid files should be single-track, with tempo and time signature metadata from the Idea or Song.

## Note Utilities (src/lib/notes.ts)
- Conversion between MIDI note numbers (0-127) and note names (C4, F#2, Bb3).
- Middle C = MIDI 60 = C4.
- Support flats and sharps in display. Store as MIDI numbers internally.
- Chord name parsing if needed for the note picker.

## Error Handling
- Wrap all Web Audio and Web MIDI operations in try/catch.
- Audio context can be suspended (autoplay policy) — always check state and resume.
- MIDI devices can disconnect mid-session — handle onStateChange events.
- Permission prompts (mic access) can be denied — show clear fallback UI.
- basic-pitch model loading can fail (network, memory) — handle gracefully with retry option.
